{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-fable-5","id":"msg_011CdsZZMxK2a98zoEg4yZE9","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01L6DKT1jLUQAg4aXuWAT4BH","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/tmp/claude-0/-home-user-creator-0/113f7cc5-237e-5d6a-8867-a97fd89c58dd/scratchpad/e6/e6-t03/primary/exec-ws/result.json","content":"{\n  \"answers\": {\n    \"2021-01-01\": \"2020-W53-5\",\n    \"2016-01-03\": \"2015-W53-7\",\n    \"2015-12-28\": \"2015-W53-1\",\n    \"2020-12-31\": \"2020-W53-4\",\n    \"2019-12-30\": \"2020-W01-1\",\n    \"2022-01-02\": \"2021-W52-7\",\n    \"2024-12-30\": \"2025-W01-1\",\n    \"2025-01-05\": \"2025-W01-7\",\n    \"2017-01-01\": \"2016-W52-7\",\n    \"2018-12-31\": \"2019-W01-1\"\n  },\n  \"method\": \"Nearest-Thursday (first-Thursday rule) method. For each date: (1) compute its Gregorian weekday (1=Mon..7=Sun) by anchoring on known Jan-1 weekdays and stepping by 365/366 mod 7 per year (Jan 1 of 2015=Thu, 2016=Fri, 2017=Sun, 2018=Mon, 2019=Tue, 2020=Wed, 2021=Fri, 2022=Sat, 2024=Mon, 2025=Wed); (2) take the Monday-based week containing the date and locate that week's Thursday; (3) the ISO week-numbering year is the calendar year of that Thursday — this is what moves boundary dates into the neighboring year's numbering; (4) the week number is the count of Thursdays in that ISO year up to and including the week's Thursday, i.e. week = (ordinal(week's Thursday) - ordinal(ISO year's first Thursday))/7 + 1; (5) the trailing digit is the date's ISO weekday 1=Mon..7=Sun. Per-item Thursdays: 2021-01-01 (Fri) -> Thu 2020-12-31, 53rd Thursday of 2020 -> 2020-W53-5; 2016-01-03 (Sun) -> Thu 2015-12-31, 53rd Thursday of 2015 -> 2015-W53-7; 2015-12-28 (Mon) -> same week -> 2015-W53-1; 2020-12-31 (Thu) -> itself, 53rd Thursday of 2020 -> 2020-W53-4; 2019-12-30 (Mon) -> Thu 2020-01-02, first Thursday of 2020 -> 2020-W01-1; 2022-01-02 (Sun) -> Thu 2021-12-30, 52nd Thursday of 2021 -> 2021-W52-7; 2024-12-30 (Mon) -> Th