{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-fable-5","id":"msg_011CdsZcTqN3oMKLF5EC2bza","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Stage S6 is complete. This trial's harness is the `isolated-child` family, so I executed the two in-session nodes (`observe-evidence`, `propose-child`) and left everything from `validate-child` onward to the root harness.\n\n**What I produced:**\n\n- **`result.json`** — the first derivation (E-A): all 10 ISO week-dates computed with the nearest-Thursday rule, method and per-item Thursday anchors stated. The boundary-sensitive results: `2021-01-01 → 2020-W53-5`, `2016-01-03 → 2015-W53-7`, `2015-12-28 → 2015-W53-1`, `2020-12-31 → 2020-W53-4`, `2019-12-30 → 2020-W01-1`, `2022-01-02 → 2021-W52-7`, `2024-12-30 → 2025-W01-1`, `2025-01-05 → 2025-W01-7`, `2017-01-01 → 2016-W52-7`, `2018-12-31 → 2019-W01-1`.\n- **`child/` bundle** (all five files, recorded in the `propose-child` propose event): an attenuated child contract matching the envelope, the four-node child harness, a standalone prompt that mandates the disjoint ordinal-date formula method (`week = floor((ordinal − weekday + 10)/7)` with week-0/week-53 boundary rules) and explicitly forbids nearest-Thursday reasoning, an input manifest containing **only** `package/artifacts/dates.json` (my derivation and all other trial artifacts are excluded to preserve the causal isolation E-B requires), and a pre-committed deterministic integration plan (role `independent_verifier`) that maps the child's answer set to a per-item agreement record by string equality, never copying child answers into the result.\n- **`resolution.json`** — Q1 `RESOLVED` (by `propose-child`, evidence in-session); Q2 `UNRESOLVED` — honestly left pending because its admissibility condition is causal and this session, as author of the first derivation, cannot satisfy it; Q3 `UNRESOLVED` — correctness is judged only by deterministic root verification.\n- **`evidence.json`** (3 records), **`result-pending.json`**, and **`execution-ledger.jsonl`** with exactly one event per in-session node (`observe`, then `propose`) in dependency order.\n\nOne deviation worth noting: only two of the five documented template files actually exist in `child-templates/` (contract and harness, under `child-*-template.json` names, found by probing since no directory-listing tool is granted); the prompt, manifest, and integration plan were authored from the shapes specified inline in `protocol.md`. My session ends here — child validation, launch, integration, and the final verified return are root-executed."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":867,"cache_read_input_tokens":61660,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":867},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6ca422d4-5d6b-4252-af3b-ea0db7bcc6a2","uuid":"177b6a53-08b0-4ef0-beb6-597007ec1ade","timestamp":"2026-08-09T17:24:05.477Z","request_id":"req_011CdsZcM7421wXyfM5NFGsA"}
